id: ops-aun4
title: Semicolon-free exported variables consume following declarations
description: "parseExportedVar has no automatic-semicolon-insertion boundary for an exported variable statement. A semicolon-free export followed on a new line by another declaration is consumed as initializer syntax, so the following binding is never judged."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-31T10:31:08.430Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-31T10:32:42.786Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-31T10:32:42.775Z"
completed_at: "2026-07-31T10:32:42.775Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 40
acceptance_criteria: "Semicolon-free export followed by another export judges both bindings; Multiline conditional, call, type, and grouped initializers are not split prematurely"
parent: ops-073p
reporter: greptile-apps
severity: high
environment: PR 33 exact head b610690
repro_steps: Analyze a documented export const first = 1 without a semicolon followed by an undocumented export const second = 2; observe only first is counted and no second violation is reported.
resolution: "Added declaration-start and expression-end token sets, stopped semicolon-free variable recovery only at a valid newline declaration boundary, and returned cleanly after an EOF-terminated final declarator."
expected_result: ASI terminates the first variable statement at a declaration boundary and the following export is independently judged.
actual_result: "Focused regression passes 2/2 together with the symlink-cycle test; two semicolon-free exports are counted independently, the undocumented second binding is reported, and a grouped multiline initializer remains intact."
component: docstring-analyzer
regression: true
customer_impact: Undocumented exports can bypass a gate advertised as fail-closed.
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-31T10:32:42.367Z","harness:codex",Variable-statement recovery needs an explicit post-loop return because the tokenizer omits an EOF token; otherwise a semicolon-free final declarator re-enters the outer declarator loop and creates a synthetic fail-closed violation.
files[1]{path,scope,note}:
  docstrings.ts,project,Exported variable statement recovery
tests[1]{command,path,scope,timeout_seconds}:
  node --test --test-name-pattern='semicolon-free exported variables' test/docstrings.test.ts,test/docstrings.test.ts,project,60
close_reason: ASI-aware declaration boundaries and EOF recovery now preserve following exports and multiline initializers.
body: ""
